title: The Mark Falls
subtitle: Prices are running away, and wages are not.
new-page: true
tags: event
view-if: year = 1921 and month = 11 and crisis = 0
max-visits: 1
priority: 6
on-arrival: inflation += 4; worker_support += 1

= The Mark Falls

In January a dollar cost sixty-five marks. In November it costs more than two hundred and fifty. Bread, potatoes and coal are rising week by week, and the wage agreements signed in spring are worth less every Friday. Industrialists like Hugo Stinnes, who borrowed in marks to buy factories, mines and newspapers, are growing richer by the day.

In Berlin there are hunger demonstrations and shops are plundered. Housewives ask the union offices what they are for.

- @committees: Form price control committees in the factories.
- @real_values: Campaign for the seizure of real values.
- @hunger: Lead the hunger demonstrations.

@committees
